 - **Lumi's harness + /memories** — out of scope until the inference host
   is proven stable; will land in a separate PR.
+
+## Installer image (bring a new box up unattended)
+
+`nix build .#installer-iso` → `result/iso/*.iso` → `dd` to a USB stick. It boots straight into
+a passwordless root shell on the console (tty1 auto-login), runs sshd with root key-only
+login for Claude's and Mimir's keys, and has iwd + networkd (DHCP on any Ethernet/Wi-Fi
+interface). Nothing network-specific is baked in; on the console:
+
+```
+iwctl device list                                  # Wi-Fi device name, e.g. wlan0
+iwctl station wlan0 scan && iwctl station wlan0 get-networks
+iwctl station wlan0 connect "<SSID>"               # prompts for the passphrase
+ip -4 addr show wlan0                              # DHCP lease from networkd (a few seconds)
+```
+Ethernet needs nothing. Then from lumi-brain: `ssh root@<ip>` and
+`nix run .#install lumi-brain2 root@<ip>`. (`tailscale up` is available as a fallback.)
+
+## PXE netboot (install box 2 over a cable, no USB stick)
+
+`modules/pxe-installer.nix` turns lumi-brain into a one-interface PXE server for the same
+installer as above, built as kernel + initrd + iPXE script (`nix build .#netboot-dir` →
+`result/{bzImage,initrd,netboot.ipxe}`, ~14 MB + ~1.4 GB). Everything it adds is scoped to
+`eno1`, the otherwise unused 2.5 GbE port: a static `10.43.0.1/24` (networkd unit `05-pxe-eno1`,
+which sorts before the `10-wan` DHCP unit), dnsmasq for DHCP + TFTP bound to that interface
+only (DNS off, `resolveLocalQueries = false`, no router/DNS options handed out), static-web-server
+on `10.43.0.1:8080` only, and firewall holes for UDP 67/69 + TCP 8080 on `eno1` only. The Wi-Fi
+uplink, `microvm-br` (which has its own DHCP server), tailscale and the kernel parameters are
+untouched. The module is enabled in `hosts/lumi-brain/default.nix` for the bring-up and should
+be switched off afterwards.
+
+Sequence on the cable: box 2's UEFI PXE client → DHCP lease + `ipxe.efi` by TFTP → iPXE
+re-DHCPs (tagged by option 175) and is handed `http://10.43.0.1:8080/netboot.ipxe` → kernel +
+initrd over HTTP → the installer boots with sshd and our keys on the lease address.
+`dhcp-ignore-clid` keys leases by MAC, so box 2 keeps one `10.43.0.x` through the firmware,
+iPXE, installer and installed-system phases.
+
+1. **On lumi-brain (once, needs root):**
+   ```sh
+   cd /home/claude-code/lumi-brain/lumi-brain
+   sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake .#lumi-brain     # builds the netboot image too (~1 min)
+   ip -4 addr show eno1                                # 10.43.0.1/24 (also while unplugged)
+   systemctl status dnsmasq static-web-server.socket   # both active
+   curl -s http://10.43.0.1:8080/netboot.ipxe          # the iPXE script
+   curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{size_download}\n' tftp://10.43.0.1/ipxe.efi   # 1198592
+   ```
+2. **Cable:** box 2's RJ45 ↔ lumi-brain's `eno1` (any straight Ethernet cable; the ports auto-cross).
+3. **Box 2 firmware setup** (Del at power-on on the EVO-X2's AMI firmware; F7 is the one-time
+   boot menu — check the splash screen):
+   - Secure Boot → **Disabled** (both the iPXE binary and the NixOS kernel are unsigned).
+   - Network Stack → Enabled, IPv4 PXE support → Enabled (IPv6 may stay off).
+   - Boot: pick `UEFI: PXE IPv4 (Realtek …)` from the one-time boot menu, or put it first in the
+     boot order. Preferred: the one-time menu — a PXE-first order will net-boot the installer
+     again after nixos-anywhere reboots the box, until the module is disabled or the cable pulled.
+   - Save & reset.
+4. **Watch the lease on lumi-brain:**
+   ```sh
+   journalctl -u dnsmasq -f            # DHCPDISCOVER/OFFER/REQUEST/ACK from box 2's MAC → 10.43.0.<n>,
+                                       # "sent /…/ipxe.efi", then a second exchange tagged "ipxe"
+   journalctl -u static-web-server -f  # GET /netboot.ipxe, /bzImage, /initrd (1.4 GB, a few seconds at 2.5 GbE)
+   ```
+   Box 2's screen: iPXE banner → kernel messages → `lumi-installer` root shell on tty1.
+   If iPXE hangs at `Configuring (net0 …)` with `ipxe.efi`, set
+   `lumi.pxeInstaller.ipxeBinary = "snp.efi"` (uses the firmware's own NIC driver) and rebuild.
+5. **Install from lumi-brain** (the host key changes between installer and installed system,
+   hence the two `-o` flags; nixos-anywhere passes them itself):
+   ```sh
+   ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no root@10.43.0.<n> \
+       lsblk -d -e7 -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL                 # /dev/nvme0n1 as in hosts/lumi-brain2/disko.nix
+   nix run /home/claude-code/lumi-brain/lumi-brain#install lumi-brain2 root@10.43.0.<n>
+   ```
+   The target is already a NixOS installer (`VARIANT_ID=installer`), so nixos-anywhere skips
+   kexec: disko partitions the disk (LUKS passphrase prompt), the `lumi-brain2` closure is built
+   on lumi-brain and copied over the cable into `/mnt`, then box 2 reboots.
+6. **After the reboot:** type the LUKS passphrase on box 2's console. Its installed config uses
+   DHCP on `en*`, so while the cable stays connected it leases from lumi-brain again — same
+   `10.43.0.<n>`, visible in `journalctl -u dnsmasq` — and `ssh mimir@10.43.0.<n>` works with the
+   keys from `modules/users.nix`. lumi-brain hands out no default route, so box 2's internet
+   comes from its own Wi-Fi (`iwctl`, see above), not via the cable. Continue with the
+   "Second box" steps below (host key into `secrets.nix`, USB4 link, weights).
+7. **Afterwards:** set `lumi.pxeInstaller.enable = false` in `hosts/lumi-brain/default.nix` (or
+   drop the import) and `sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake .#lumi-brain`; `eno1` returns to the
+   plain `10-wan` DHCP-client behaviour. Leaving it on is harmless if the cable is still the
+   handy path to box 2 before the USB4 link is up.
+
+## Second box (lumi-brain2)
+
+Same flake, second `nixosConfiguration`. Differences live in `hosts/lumi-brain2/`:
+hostname, 128 GB GTT/TTM sizing, and a plaintext ext4 `/weights` partition next to the
+LUKS root. Both hosts import `modules/interconnect.nix` (USB4 host-to-host networking:
+`thunderbolt-net`, static `10.99.0.1/30` ↔ `10.99.0.2/30` on `thunderbolt0`, MTU 65520,
+`iperf3` + `bolt`).
+
+Bring-up:
+1. Boot the installer on the new box, confirm `/dev/nvme0n1` and the disk split in
+   `hosts/lumi-brain2/disko.nix`.
+2. `nix run .#install lumi-brain2 root@<ip>`.
+3. Add the new host's SSH host key (`/persist/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub`) to `secrets.nix`
+   and re-key the `.age` files it needs, then `nixos-rebuild switch --flake .#lumi-brain2`.
+4. Plug the USB4 cable; on each box `boltctl list` then `boltctl authorize <uuid>` once;
+   `ip link show thunderbolt0`; then measure: `iperf3 -s` / `iperf3 -c 10.99.0.x -P 1` and `-P 4`,
+   `ping -c 200 -i 0.005 10.99.0.x`, and the engine's request/reply pattern with
+   `deepstrix/scripts/netbench/rtt_pingpong.py` (32 KB, p50/p99). Repeat with MTU 1500.
+5. `rsync` the DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash HF snapshot to `/weights/` and point
+   `~/.cache/deepstrix/models/dsv4.1f` at it.
